■ FSCHRHUNT
PROJECT: code

///

STATUS: DEVELOPMENT

///

OVERVIEW:
 - One folder for Git work: repos/<repo> for clones, worktrees/<agent>-<repo> for tasks.
 - A small Bash wrapper over ordinary Git: new, list, remove, upgrade.
 - No index, no daemon, no configuration. The root defaults to ~/Code.

///

INSTALL:
 curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fschrhunt/code/main/scripts/install.sh | sh

START:
 git clone https://github.com/fschrhunt/e.git ~/Code/repos/e
 cd ~/Code/repos/e
 code new pi
 # → ~/Code/worktrees/pi-e
 code list
 code remove pi-e

///

NOTES:
 - new names the worktree <agent>-<repo>, detached; name the branch from the work.
 - Each worktree carries one branch and one task.
 - remove keeps the branch; delete it with ordinary Git when you mean to.
 - upgrade updates Code itself.

///

